## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

This is a textbook **coverage-farming** test suite. Every production method is called (→ 95% line coverage), but almost nothing is actually verified. These tests will pass even if every method returns wrong results or silently corrupts data.

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — Missing Assertions (Coverage Without Verification)

**1. `AddProduct_Works` (line 17) — Fire-and-forget, zero assertions**
Calls `AddProduct` but never checks the product was stored.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var stored = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(stored);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", stored.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, stored.Price);
```

**2. `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 32) — Calls update, never checks the new price**
The production `UpdatePrice` could save the *old* price or any garbage — this test would still pass.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
```

**3. `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 38) — Calls remove, never checks deletion**
Product could still be in the store and this test passes fine.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

**4. `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63) — No assertion at all, empty catalog**
Doesn't assert the count, and tests against an empty store so it doesn't even exercise a meaningful code path.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-002", "Gadget", 19.99m));
Assert.AreEqual(2, _catalog.GetProductCount());
```

**5. `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68) — No assertion on discounted prices**
A 10% discount is applied but never checked. `ApplyBulkDiscount` could multiply by 0 or noop entirely.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002")!.Price);
```

**6. `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 84) — No assertion that imported products exist**
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
var product = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(product);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", product.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, product.Price);
```

